Off by default. With VLLM_EMBED_UVA=1 the packed embedding table (weight_packed, from
qwen3_5-embed-quant) of the main model and the MTP module is moved to pinned host memory after the
weights load and read through a CUDA UVA view. A decode step pulls one row per request over PCIe, and the
freed VRAM goes to the KV pool: +32,143 tokens (204,336 to 236,479, +15.7%) at SPEC=mtp CTX=long on a
3090 (PCIe 4.0 x16) with decode and prefill unchanged, for about 2.1 GiB of host RAM and 20 s of boot.
Skipped for tied embeddings, whose lm_head would read the whole table from host RAM every step, and for
a table that is not quantized (a warning says so). The knob is registered in envs.py so it sits in the
torch.compile cache key. Based on a script by @rodrigocsousa (syv-ai/HyperQwen#281), who measured it first
on two RTX 3060s (155k to 200k context).

Kind: feature
What: `VLLM_EMBED_UVA=1` keeps the quantized token embedding (main model and MTP module) in pinned host RAM
  behind a CUDA UVA view, freeing about 1.25 GiB of VRAM for the KV pool (+15.7% tokens on a 3090) at no
  measured decode or prefill cost, for about 2.1 GiB of host RAM; default off
Upstream: none
Cut-against: 0.32.0: adjacency with #60623, which removed the vendored qwen3_5 configs (transformers >= 5.16.1
  ships them)
Retires-when: stays while the knob exists

